WEBVTT

00:50.383 --> 00:52.302
You see, the thing about dating

00:52.969 --> 00:55.138
is that it's like living
in a different world.

00:56.681 --> 00:58.183
Most especially

00:58.975 --> 01:00.518
dating Yeon-su

01:01.019 --> 01:03.855
is a completely different world.

01:06.066 --> 01:08.068
Ung!

01:08.151 --> 01:08.985
Yeah?

01:09.778 --> 01:10.737
What?

01:12.322 --> 01:13.281
What is it?

01:17.535 --> 01:19.287
- Why'd you call me?
- It's your bedtime.

01:19.370 --> 01:20.455
Hmm?

01:21.372 --> 01:23.583
I can't sleep now. It's only 10 p.m.

01:27.003 --> 01:30.006
I drank all the jujube tea.
Where did you get this from?

01:30.673 --> 01:33.510
- Does this house have a well?
- Drink it and go to bed.

01:34.135 --> 01:37.722
Uh, I don't sleep at this hour.
Even kids don't sleep this early.

01:37.806 --> 01:39.808
So should I sleep here then?

01:47.941 --> 01:49.609
We should sleep when it's dark.

01:49.692 --> 01:52.320
It's dangerous for you
to walk around at this late hour.

01:55.323 --> 01:56.491
Let's go to bed.

01:59.744 --> 02:00.620
Come on!

02:00.703 --> 02:02.205
Wake up!

02:02.288 --> 02:04.999
Make up your mind.
Do you want me to sleep or not?

02:05.083 --> 02:07.502
You can't sleep at night
because you sleep in the morning.

02:07.585 --> 02:10.380
You have to endure this
to get a normal sleep cycle.

02:10.463 --> 02:11.381
Okay?

02:13.508 --> 02:15.260
But as you're all aware,

02:15.343 --> 02:17.679
that world isn't really a good fit for me.

02:19.389 --> 02:21.182
But hey, what can I do?

02:21.266 --> 02:23.309
Oh, the bus is here. See you around.

02:23.393 --> 02:24.769
Oh, wait, Yeon-su!

02:28.648 --> 02:29.732
See you.

02:29.816 --> 02:31.276
- Yeon-su.
- Yeah?

02:32.735 --> 02:34.195
Bye.

02:47.709 --> 02:48.585
What's up?

02:49.294 --> 02:51.421
I just got back home after work.

02:51.504 --> 02:53.715
You got off work late.
Did you have dinner already?

02:53.798 --> 02:56.092
Mm-hmm, I ate at the place
you recommended to me,

02:56.176 --> 02:57.093
and it was pretty good.

02:57.177 --> 02:59.679
- Let's go there next time.
- Okay, let's do that.

02:59.762 --> 03:02.390
Back then and even now…

03:10.023 --> 03:12.066
…I want to keep living in this world.

03:14.319 --> 03:15.653
A world without an end,

03:16.654 --> 03:17.614
forever.

03:19.115 --> 03:20.033
No.

03:20.116 --> 03:21.784
But you're the only one

03:22.619 --> 03:23.995
that I can get rid of.

03:24.078 --> 03:25.496
Give me a reason.

03:26.206 --> 03:28.583
Give me just one reason
why we can't be together!

03:36.633 --> 03:38.092
Those are useless thoughts.

03:40.970 --> 03:43.056
LIKE WATER FOR CHOCOLATE

03:45.433 --> 03:47.477
In times like these,
I have to be more cautious.

03:47.560 --> 03:48.645
THE LIKELIHOOD OF STAYING IN
A RELATIONSHIP WITH YOUR EX

03:48.728 --> 03:51.856
Because misfortune always comes
disguised as happiness.

03:54.317 --> 03:59.280
"Couples who fight often have
a higher chance of dating again."

04:01.282 --> 04:06.162
"However, they think that they will still
be the same after they get back together

04:06.829 --> 04:09.165
and have lower expectations
of each other."

04:10.083 --> 04:12.085
"In order to maintain your relationship,

04:12.669 --> 04:16.172
you must show your partner
new sides of yourself

04:16.256 --> 04:20.593
to break such expectations.
This is necessary."

04:23.388 --> 04:26.557
I shouldn't lower my ground
just because everything is okay.

04:27.850 --> 04:32.272
So I believe that I have to prepare myself
for any possible risks that might happen.

04:32.939 --> 04:35.191
"New sides of myself…"

04:35.275 --> 04:36.526
I went through so much to get here.

04:38.987 --> 04:41.155
I can't repeat the same mistakes again.

04:55.837 --> 05:01.009
EPISODE 13

05:07.307 --> 05:09.350
I wanna stay with you forever.

05:10.101 --> 05:11.728
Come here.

05:23.406 --> 05:24.490
What do we do?

05:25.783 --> 05:27.785
I'll deal with him. You go to work.

05:27.869 --> 05:28.745
What will you do?

05:29.370 --> 05:31.080
Is there a brick here somewhere?

05:31.789 --> 05:34.083
Take care of this quietly
so there's no fuss.

05:34.167 --> 05:36.294
- Mm. Hmm.
- Bye.

05:44.886 --> 05:46.763
Ung… Ung…

05:49.057 --> 05:52.477
Hey, inhale with your nose,
exhale through your mouth.

05:59.776 --> 06:01.527
What… what was that about?

06:02.403 --> 06:03.237
It just happened.

06:03.905 --> 06:05.073
"It just happened"?

06:05.156 --> 06:06.574
Hey, don't overreact.

06:07.658 --> 06:10.787
Wait, since when?
Since when have you been doing this?

06:11.871 --> 06:13.915
So you didn't let me come
to your house because…

06:14.832 --> 06:17.085
No, forget all that.

06:17.168 --> 06:19.462
Who else knows about this?
Does Ji-ung know?

06:21.714 --> 06:23.049
And what about Sol-i?

06:24.300 --> 06:25.176
Probably.

06:26.761 --> 06:30.098
- And what about your parents?
- Yeah, they know.

06:30.932 --> 06:34.268
- Wait, is that even important?
- I'm ashamed, you know.

06:34.352 --> 06:37.730
Ashamed. How could you
not tell me about any of this?

06:38.231 --> 06:39.065
How could you?

06:39.649 --> 06:41.818
- Are you crying?
- How could you do this?

06:42.443 --> 06:45.279
- I can't believe this!
- Have you lost it? Eun-ho!

06:47.073 --> 06:48.408
Good morning, everyone.

06:48.491 --> 06:50.034
- Good morning, Ms. Kook.
- Good morning.

06:52.245 --> 06:54.705
Hey, you think
she's going to text him again?

06:54.789 --> 06:56.666
- Keep it down.
- I think she will.

06:57.375 --> 07:00.753
I couldn't take care of Eun-ho.
I'll wait for my next chance.

07:07.218 --> 07:08.636
Ms. Kook.

07:09.387 --> 07:10.555
Oh, Mr. Bang.

07:11.222 --> 07:13.141
So tell me, do you have good news?

07:13.641 --> 07:15.435
Oh, no, there's nothing.

07:15.518 --> 07:17.770
But a double negative makes a positive.

07:18.771 --> 07:20.731
Hold on. Why are you whispering?

07:22.400 --> 07:24.944
There have been rumors going around.

07:26.946 --> 07:28.197
What kind of rumors?

07:28.698 --> 07:31.576
Rumors of you dating someone.

07:38.458 --> 07:39.834
Who would say that?

07:42.086 --> 07:45.089
No, it's all right.
Don't get worked up over it. Okay?

07:45.173 --> 07:48.468
The rumors were so terrible sounding
that I told everyone it wasn't true.

07:49.051 --> 07:50.178
"Ms. Kook isn't someone like that."

07:50.261 --> 07:52.972
"She's not someone
who has any love for humanity."

07:53.055 --> 07:55.016
"Therefore, she's not human."

07:57.310 --> 07:58.853
That's not why I'm here, though.

07:59.520 --> 08:02.773
I received a call from Soen, they asked
if they could check the footage.

08:02.857 --> 08:06.110
To be exact, the one of the project
they filmed for the documentary.

08:06.194 --> 08:08.070
Yes, and I'm quite curious too.

08:08.154 --> 08:10.531
They must have filmed our company as well.

08:10.615 --> 08:12.033
Yes, I'll ask them about it.

08:12.116 --> 08:14.785
When does it premier again?
I assume it's going to be soon?

08:15.828 --> 08:19.165
Oh, by the way,
I did an interview with them.

08:19.248 --> 08:21.375
Tell them to please let it air

08:21.459 --> 08:23.961
without editing it out, okay?

08:26.005 --> 08:26.839
Very good.

08:39.810 --> 08:41.062
KIM JI-UNG

08:44.982 --> 08:47.610
The person you're calling
is unavailable…

08:50.154 --> 08:54.116
HOW IS EDITING GOING?

08:57.119 --> 08:58.829
I guess he's busy.

09:02.375 --> 09:05.211
Well, we could agree
on a schedule for that.

09:06.546 --> 09:07.672
The question though, is…

09:07.755 --> 09:09.507
will he be able to do it?

09:10.675 --> 09:12.468
END OF FIRST DRAFT
PREVIEW TO BE ADDED

09:17.890 --> 09:18.766
PD. Kim.

09:20.935 --> 09:22.687
I see you've found your direction.

09:24.981 --> 09:27.024
If this is the first draft,
it'll be great.

09:28.109 --> 09:31.445
Good job. I always knew
that you could do it.

09:31.529 --> 09:33.906
I'm going to fix the last narration part.
I don't like it.

09:33.990 --> 09:35.074
Sure, go ahead.

09:35.157 --> 09:37.743
Hey, how come they look like
they haven't changed a single bit, huh?

09:37.827 --> 09:39.245
They both seem so young and lively.

09:39.328 --> 09:43.040
And there's some tension between them too.
I'm curious about the next episode.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.834
All right. I'm satisfied.

09:45.459 --> 09:46.294
That's a relief.

09:47.378 --> 09:49.005
Now stop chasing me around for it.

09:49.088 --> 09:50.214
All right.

09:50.298 --> 09:53.676
It's not normal for the leader
to beg his team to see their work.

09:53.759 --> 09:55.261
Do you think so? How about you?

09:56.262 --> 09:58.055
It's ridiculous.

09:58.139 --> 10:00.182
Now then, what are you doing after work?

10:00.266 --> 10:03.227
We should celebrate.
After all, the first draft is finished.

10:03.311 --> 10:04.562
I still have work to do.

10:05.146 --> 10:07.815
Hey, what could be so urgent?
Let's have fun!

10:07.898 --> 10:10.943
The leader shouldn't be saying that.
I'm going to the editing room.

10:19.452 --> 10:20.286
Is he okay?

10:21.120 --> 10:22.455
Huh?

10:23.164 --> 10:24.332
Did you see his eyes?

10:25.374 --> 10:27.001
He seems to have lost his mind.

10:29.295 --> 10:31.756
Make sure he eats his meal on time.

10:31.839 --> 10:34.842
You should be eating well
when you're hurting inside.

10:34.925 --> 10:37.428
Got it. I'll make sure he eats well.

10:38.012 --> 10:42.058
Hey, you, you should be taking care of me.
I've been feeling so lonely lately.

10:42.141 --> 10:44.018
I'm always wandering around by myself.

10:44.101 --> 10:46.687
And what's wrong with Ji-ung?
He's just busy.

10:46.771 --> 10:50.191
He thinks he's the only one
with a lot of work? We all do!

10:50.274 --> 10:51.233
EDITING ROOM

11:18.969 --> 11:22.223
Can you tell us
what the new special documentary is about?

11:22.306 --> 11:24.684
Next year is my tenth debut anniversary.

11:24.767 --> 11:28.688
To commemorate the occasion, I'm preparing
a special video to show all of my fans.

11:28.771 --> 11:30.856
So it has been ten years already.

11:30.940 --> 11:34.193
Oh, you must be feeling
so many emotions right now.

11:35.152 --> 11:36.904
Yes, I do.

11:37.863 --> 11:39.740
I have quite a lot on my mind.

11:39.824 --> 11:45.079
Now, lastly, I do believe that a lot
of people are quite curious about this--

11:45.162 --> 11:46.122
The scandal?

11:47.456 --> 11:50.543
I hope you don't mind.
I know this may be a sensitive topic,

11:50.626 --> 11:53.421
but could you reveal anything about that
to the viewers of Litte

11:53.504 --> 11:55.589
who are watching this show live right now?

11:55.673 --> 11:57.550
Sure. I don't see any harm in it.

11:58.759 --> 12:02.388
Is there any truth to the rumors
that your two are dating right now?

12:02.471 --> 12:04.890
No, we aren't dating.

12:06.475 --> 12:07.476
But I do like him.

12:09.103 --> 12:11.939
- What?
- As a fan, of course.

12:12.022 --> 12:13.357
Oh.

12:13.441 --> 12:16.485
At first, he said
that he was a big fan of mine.

12:16.569 --> 12:18.779
But it turns out, I'm the bigger fan.

12:18.863 --> 12:20.531
So I wanted to become his friend,

12:21.365 --> 12:24.577
but I feel we became awkward
after the article came out.

12:26.537 --> 12:30.332
So to everyone watching,
don't make accusations about us.

12:30.416 --> 12:31.709
That's all I ask of you.

12:33.127 --> 12:35.254
So NJ was a victim of all this.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.298
And all because of that traitor.

12:37.381 --> 12:39.008
Hey, stay on one stance.

12:39.091 --> 12:42.178
If you're going to be angry,
do it at home. Why are you even here?

12:42.803 --> 12:46.307
Well, I'm here to do my job,
so I have to breathe the same air as you.

12:46.974 --> 12:49.852
By the way, how are the preparations
for your exhibition coming along?

12:50.436 --> 12:53.147
I got a lot done.
Am I ever behind schedule?

12:55.316 --> 12:57.902
Okay, what is it?
What are you even looking at?

12:59.195 --> 13:00.863
- Well, who knows?
- What?

13:00.946 --> 13:03.824
You could neglect your drawings,
after all, you're dating.

13:04.492 --> 13:07.077
- Stop that.
- Can you even focus on your work?

13:07.161 --> 13:09.914
I know that you're the kind
to neglect everything when you're dating.

13:09.997 --> 13:11.582
- Eun-ho, stop it--
- I don't get it.

13:11.665 --> 13:14.502
I just don't get
why you're seeing Yeon-su again.

13:14.585 --> 13:15.419
What?

13:15.503 --> 13:18.172
You were in so much pain.
Do you wanna repeat it?

13:18.255 --> 13:21.050
Did you forget how many times
you went through this?

13:21.133 --> 13:23.928
Do I have to remind you
how bad things got each time?

13:24.512 --> 13:27.139
I don't want to go through that again.

13:36.649 --> 13:37.483
What?

13:38.567 --> 13:39.568
Hey.

13:47.034 --> 13:50.830
Come on, don't say it like that.
It's fine. I'll take care of myself.

13:51.789 --> 13:54.583
How should I believe you?
You weren't going to tell me anyway.

13:54.667 --> 13:56.752
I'm really sorry about that.

13:56.836 --> 13:58.420
But I… I…

14:01.131 --> 14:03.217
It's just, I was such
in a good mood lately.

14:04.593 --> 14:06.720
I'm so happy right now. What can I do?

14:11.141 --> 14:13.018
Oh, gross.

14:14.770 --> 14:16.939
Well, things will be different this time.

14:17.022 --> 14:18.649
I won't mess this up, okay?

14:25.447 --> 14:26.824
Man, I'm hungry.

14:27.533 --> 14:28.742
Shall we go eat?

14:31.662 --> 14:33.247
Do you wanna talk about work?

14:36.083 --> 14:40.212
How about we talk about
that thing you mentioned. A raise, right?

14:44.633 --> 14:46.302
What about a raise?

14:53.267 --> 14:56.562
Anyway, I'll be
watching over you, you two.

14:59.523 --> 15:01.650
- I want 30 percent.
- What?

15:03.485 --> 15:05.195
Okay, 25 percent.

15:09.617 --> 15:10.451
20.

15:30.220 --> 15:31.555
Have you eaten?

15:31.639 --> 15:34.600
Yes, I have. You should eat too.

15:37.144 --> 15:38.646
UNG

15:38.729 --> 15:40.105
- What are you doing?
- I'm meeting.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.690
- I'm at a restaurant.
- Okay.

15:41.774 --> 15:44.485
- Did you finish work?
- Not yet. i'll be done soon.

15:44.568 --> 15:45.903
YES, OKAY, NOT TODAY

15:46.403 --> 15:48.697
Were my replies too simple?

15:48.781 --> 15:50.950
YOUR NEW SIDE

15:51.533 --> 15:55.245
If I want to find a new side,
then I need to learn from new people.

15:55.913 --> 15:58.290
Dating? Well, it's no big deal.

15:58.374 --> 16:00.793
If a man and a woman like each other,
they date,

16:00.876 --> 16:03.295
and the, well, they both kiss,

16:03.379 --> 16:04.546
and then…

16:10.678 --> 16:12.972
And then they say, "I love you."

16:14.181 --> 16:16.266
No, that's not a good example.

16:18.894 --> 16:21.146
Did you enjoy your lunch today, Ms. Kook?

16:21.230 --> 16:22.773
Oh, yes.

16:31.699 --> 16:32.950
Hey, Ye-in.

16:33.033 --> 16:34.034
Yes?

16:34.618 --> 16:36.745
- Do you have a boyfriend?
- Me?

16:37.913 --> 16:41.208
I don't, why? Is there someone
you wanna set me up with?

16:42.001 --> 16:44.336
Then did you have any boyfriends before?

16:45.004 --> 16:47.673
Mm. Of course I did.

16:47.756 --> 16:49.717
A had quite a lot back then.

16:50.551 --> 16:51.510
So…

16:52.136 --> 16:56.223
would you…
consider yourself to be good at dating?

16:58.475 --> 17:01.562
Well, it might seem weird
for me to say this,

17:01.645 --> 17:04.440
but if I were evaluated
for my ability in dating,

17:04.523 --> 17:08.819
I guess I would be the CEO
of this company by now.

17:08.902 --> 17:10.988
- Oh.
- Why do you ask?

17:12.906 --> 17:13.782
Well…

17:16.201 --> 17:20.789
How exactly do you date a person properly?

17:24.960 --> 17:27.337
Well, I think you came
to the right place, Ms. Kook.

17:45.481 --> 17:48.901
I'm getting off of work soon.
Shall we go on a date?

17:49.401 --> 17:51.737
Okay. I'll pick you up. Wait there.

18:06.001 --> 18:10.339
SUPERB CREATIVE CENTER

18:24.103 --> 18:24.937
Hi there.

18:28.607 --> 18:29.900
Oh, hi.

18:30.651 --> 18:33.403
Oh, wait.
You're wearing different clothes.

18:33.487 --> 18:37.741
Oh, I accidentally spilled something
so I bought new clothes.

18:37.825 --> 18:39.993
Oh. Did you spill a lot or something?

18:40.869 --> 18:42.329
- Let's go.
- Hmm.

18:53.590 --> 18:57.136
Firstly, visual stimulation
is very important.

18:57.219 --> 19:00.305
You have to show different styles
every now and then so that

19:00.389 --> 19:03.308
you can get a kind of tension
flowing between you two.

19:18.407 --> 19:21.034
You know what, I still think
it would have been much better

19:21.118 --> 19:22.828
to just hit Eun-ho with a brick.

19:22.911 --> 19:25.497
Ugh, it was hard
having to deal with his sulking.

19:26.165 --> 19:29.126
 Now this is very, very important.

19:29.209 --> 19:33.547
Reaction. I found out that guys are crazy
for people who give good reactions.

19:33.630 --> 19:36.300
I dated so many guys using my reactions.

19:36.383 --> 19:38.886
React to what he does. And always smile.

19:38.969 --> 19:41.972
Now why in the world would he be so sulky?

19:42.055 --> 19:44.183
I swear, sometimes
he can be so weird, you know.

19:44.266 --> 19:46.018
- He must like me so much--
- Oh!

19:46.560 --> 19:49.229
- Really?
- Huh? Yeah.

19:51.190 --> 19:52.232
That's so funny.

19:52.733 --> 19:53.901
What is?

19:55.527 --> 19:56.653
Huh? What's what?

19:56.737 --> 19:58.280
- What?
- Huh?

20:00.741 --> 20:03.035
And compliment him
as many times as you can.

20:04.453 --> 20:05.829
Hey, you're such a good driver…

20:07.414 --> 20:08.540
Oh, sorry about that.

20:09.249 --> 20:11.460
What did you say? I didn't catch that.

20:11.543 --> 20:12.794
It's nothing.

20:15.881 --> 20:19.218
They love receiving compliments,
even for the smallest of things.

20:20.385 --> 20:22.763
You have really large hands.

20:22.846 --> 20:24.348
What? That was random.

20:24.431 --> 20:26.183
You know, they're so big.

20:26.808 --> 20:28.143
As in, they're huge.

20:28.936 --> 20:29.811
Oh.

20:31.730 --> 20:32.898
Right.

20:49.331 --> 20:50.540
You sure about this?

20:50.624 --> 20:52.918
You usually prefer Korean food.

20:53.001 --> 20:55.963
Well, sometimes I crave
for food like this too.

20:56.046 --> 20:57.339
Ah.

20:57.422 --> 21:00.676
I begged you for a month to go eat pasta
when we were in university.

21:00.759 --> 21:03.428
- But you never said yes.
- Wait, really?

21:04.805 --> 21:06.932
Well, people's tastes do change.

21:07.849 --> 21:08.684
Hmm.

21:09.810 --> 21:12.604
- I'll cut this for you.
- No, I'll do it. It's closer to me anyway.

21:12.688 --> 21:14.147
- No, let me do it.
- No.

21:17.359 --> 21:18.443
Oh.

21:22.406 --> 21:25.659
And nagging.
Nagging is a big no-no, Ms. Kook!

21:26.243 --> 21:28.996
Men especially despise it
when you nag them.

21:31.790 --> 21:32.958
Oh, I'm sorry.

21:33.041 --> 21:35.544
Waiter, can I get
a wet towel over here, please.

21:35.627 --> 21:38.714
It's fine. I'll wipe it myself.
It's okay, really.

21:38.797 --> 21:43.510
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Uh, are you sure it'll come off?

21:43.593 --> 21:45.387
It's fine. I'll just have it dry cleaned.

21:45.470 --> 21:47.389
Why did it have to fly there?

21:47.472 --> 21:48.890
- You should've put…
- You should've just…

21:49.725 --> 21:52.602
I mean, I mean this.
I should have put this here.

21:53.812 --> 21:55.188
It was my bad.

22:00.068 --> 22:01.695
- Hey, Ung.
- Huh?

22:01.778 --> 22:04.364
- Eat up, now. Ah.
- Oh.

22:06.158 --> 22:07.951
- Is it good?
- Hmm.

22:08.618 --> 22:10.037
Hm.

22:27.971 --> 22:29.639
What are you thinking about?

22:29.723 --> 22:31.767
It's been a long while
since we walked like this

22:31.850 --> 22:34.269
instead of running after each other.

22:34.353 --> 22:35.187
What?

22:36.188 --> 22:40.317
You used to say that walking
without a purpose was too inefficient,

22:40.400 --> 22:42.569
that's why we always ran around back then.

22:43.570 --> 22:45.781
- Did I really say that?
- Hmm.

22:46.573 --> 22:49.368
I think we were the only ones
who ran around Deoksugung Palace.

22:50.869 --> 22:53.872
I was really obsessed
with efficiency back then.

22:53.955 --> 22:55.415
It was messy.

22:56.625 --> 22:59.086
That's not true. You were so cool.

23:00.462 --> 23:02.089
And the last thing you must do…

23:02.172 --> 23:05.258
is to make sure you make
a romantic vibe every chance you get.

23:05.342 --> 23:07.052
Dating is all about

23:07.886 --> 23:09.346
having butterflies.

23:16.853 --> 23:19.981
By the way,
there's not a lot of people here.

23:21.233 --> 23:23.693
You're right.
It's not even that late yet, though.

23:24.277 --> 23:26.571
How is it that there's nobody around here?

23:31.701 --> 23:32.661
Oh…

23:43.422 --> 23:45.048
Ah. Ow.

23:45.132 --> 23:47.426
What was that for?

23:48.969 --> 23:51.680
- What are you doing, Yeon-su?
- What do you mean?

23:51.763 --> 23:55.100
What's gotten into you today?
What's this character you're playing?

23:56.518 --> 23:58.562
You've been acting so weird all day.

23:59.980 --> 24:01.606
What is it that you're plotting?

24:01.690 --> 24:03.358
I'm not plotting anything.

24:03.442 --> 24:06.069
- I was just making an effort, that's all.
- What effort?

24:06.987 --> 24:09.656
I'm was trying to make
this relationship go well.

24:09.739 --> 24:10.699
Huh?

24:11.283 --> 24:13.452
Can't you see that
I'm trying to change for you

24:13.535 --> 24:15.871
so that we'll stop fighting
like we did before?

24:15.954 --> 24:18.123
Why do you have to do that?

24:18.206 --> 24:19.958
So that we won't ever break up.

24:20.584 --> 24:23.003
They say that
couples who fight and break up often

24:23.086 --> 24:24.713
have a higher chance of breaking up again.

24:24.796 --> 24:28.884
And that they know each other so much
that they have no expectations.

24:28.967 --> 24:30.385
Who said that?

24:30.469 --> 24:33.346
Dr. Yoo Yeong, Hankook University's
relationship psychologist.

24:33.847 --> 24:34.931
But that person doesn't know you.

24:36.433 --> 24:37.309
What?

24:37.392 --> 24:40.270
There are so many people like you
who are always different each time.

24:41.855 --> 24:44.441
You always feel new. And different.

24:44.524 --> 24:46.651
You're different
from when I saw you yesterday.

24:48.695 --> 24:49.946
That's not what I mean.

24:50.030 --> 24:51.907
See? Another side.

24:51.990 --> 24:54.451
- You're different from three seconds ago.
- Stop.

24:55.410 --> 24:57.579
I never thought
that you were so predictable.

24:57.662 --> 25:00.665
I mean, if that were possible,
I'd be the one with a Ph. D. here.

25:02.334 --> 25:04.085
Okay, but still,

25:04.169 --> 25:07.255
I felt I've always been
such a nag with you

25:07.339 --> 25:10.300
and that I was always the one
starting the fights between us,

25:10.383 --> 25:12.552
so I was trying to stop that.

25:14.137 --> 25:16.681
I like you for who you are.

25:18.266 --> 25:21.144
I like that you always have
new things to nag about.

25:23.772 --> 25:26.650
Even so, I don't want to hear
the same nagging.

25:27.567 --> 25:29.945
You'll have to come up with new things
for the rest of your life.

25:30.862 --> 25:31.947
Do you mean that?

25:36.326 --> 25:38.245
I guess this means I ruined our date.

25:38.328 --> 25:39.621
It can start over.

25:40.413 --> 25:42.249
Okay. So why don't we go do
what you want now?

25:43.667 --> 25:45.085
All right. Let's go.

25:52.926 --> 25:54.636
Guide me to Hwiyeong-dong, please.

25:54.719 --> 25:56.721
GUIDE ME TO HWIYEONG-DONG PLEASE

25:56.805 --> 25:59.975
We're going back home now?
You don't want to do anything else?

26:00.058 --> 26:01.017
There is.

26:15.115 --> 26:18.535
- Is this what you wanted to do?
- Hmm, I love this the most.

26:19.244 --> 26:22.163
Going to the neighborhood pub
in the middle of cold weather

26:22.247 --> 26:25.041
and chatting the night away
over hot fishcake stew.

26:25.125 --> 26:27.294
You're right. I love this the most too.

26:30.213 --> 26:31.631
You two are ridiculous.

26:31.715 --> 26:35.635
If you're going to shamelessly
stay here all night over one menu item,

26:35.719 --> 26:37.721
at least give the pub owner a glance.

26:38.555 --> 26:41.224
Sol-i, this is kind of spicy.
Ung can't eat spicy food.

26:41.308 --> 26:42.934
Mm. I'll be fine.

26:43.018 --> 26:44.894
I got used to it
after eating with Yeon-su.

26:44.978 --> 26:47.814
- How about something not spicy?
- Uh, okay…

26:47.897 --> 26:49.357
Order what you wanna eat, Yeon-su.

26:52.652 --> 26:55.822
Wow. You're the first customers
that make me wanna puke.

26:56.990 --> 26:59.159
Good job holding it in, Sol-i.

26:59.242 --> 27:00.243
Hang in there.

27:01.244 --> 27:03.246
Business isn't easy, you know.

27:03.330 --> 27:04.581
You got this, Sol-i.

27:15.717 --> 27:17.218
- You want a fish cake?
- Hmm.

27:17.302 --> 27:18.178
Here.

27:20.722 --> 27:22.432
- Careful.
- It looks good.

27:22.515 --> 27:24.476
All right.

27:29.648 --> 27:31.232
Is it hot?

27:48.083 --> 27:51.002
You startled me.
What do you want, Grandma?

27:51.086 --> 27:52.921
When did you get home last night?

27:54.089 --> 27:55.465
I don't really know.

27:55.548 --> 27:58.385
You little brat!

28:00.512 --> 28:02.764
Were you with Ung
the entire time last night?

28:03.640 --> 28:05.225
Well, I was.

28:05.308 --> 28:08.311
But I didn't arrive home
that late, Grandma. Honest.

28:08.395 --> 28:12.023
Are you really going to go
all the way with him?

28:12.107 --> 28:14.150
What? How can you say that, Grandma?

28:14.234 --> 28:16.986
I'm always going to stay here
by your side.

28:17.070 --> 28:18.822
Stop goofing around, will you?

28:19.406 --> 28:22.325
Listen, if you really want to be together
with Choi Ung that much,

28:22.409 --> 28:24.119
then you just bring him here instead.

28:24.202 --> 28:26.955
Grandma, you'll only
make him uncomfortable, you know.

28:27.038 --> 28:29.374
Last time I brought him here,
you totally bullied him.

28:29.457 --> 28:33.670
Well, that's because I was trying to know
what he thinks about your relationship.

28:33.753 --> 28:36.005
Why are you so old-fashioned, Grandma?

28:36.089 --> 28:38.216
You're getting ahead of yourself. Hm.

28:38.299 --> 28:39.634
I'm taking a shower.

28:40.301 --> 28:44.514
Oh, and don't even think
about going to see Ung. Okay?

28:44.597 --> 28:47.267
'Cause I'll die of embarrassment
if you do that.

28:47.851 --> 28:48.852
What the…

28:49.686 --> 28:52.188
How dare she talk to me like that?

28:54.315 --> 28:56.776
Mm-hmm. You should head to work.
You'll be late.

28:56.860 --> 28:58.987
Don't make me drink on a weekday again.

28:59.070 --> 29:02.741
Oh? Hey, you were the one who asked
to drink another bottle at the end.

29:02.824 --> 29:04.868
Stop. Don't ever mention last night.

29:05.535 --> 29:08.830
- I should get going now. See you around.
- Okay.

30:13.770 --> 30:15.980
I saw the interview you did.

30:16.564 --> 30:18.358
And the article that came out today.

30:18.441 --> 30:22.529
I thought I should at least thank you
for being so considerate and thoughtful.

30:22.612 --> 30:24.739
So, thank you, NJ.

30:24.823 --> 30:27.325
He's drawing a line between us again.

30:56.229 --> 30:59.983
I finally got one text after so many days,
and you wanna call him right away?

31:01.025 --> 31:02.652
There's no way I'm that cheap.

31:03.361 --> 31:05.613
Let's just ignore that, shall we?

31:29.178 --> 31:30.305
Oh, darn it.

31:57.206 --> 32:00.168
Come on, Dad,
why did you order so many cabbages?

32:00.877 --> 32:03.379
Well, why else do you think I did, huh?

32:03.463 --> 32:05.632
It's the season of making kimchi.
Did you forget that?

32:05.715 --> 32:07.508
Oh, that's right. I forgot.

32:07.592 --> 32:10.637
I think I have a fever,
I need to go home and rest.

32:10.720 --> 32:12.221
Oh, okay.

32:12.305 --> 32:13.514
Go on home and rest.

32:13.598 --> 32:15.266
But make sure you come back tomorrow.

32:15.350 --> 32:16.935
That's when the cabbages will be here.

32:17.018 --> 32:20.647
Oh, man. Are you making kimchi
for the entire neighborhood?

32:20.730 --> 32:22.899
Hey, Dad. I think you should downsize.

32:22.982 --> 32:24.567
Downsize your restaurants too.

32:24.651 --> 32:27.612
Your business will fail if you keep
trying to many things at once.

32:27.695 --> 32:31.658
What are you going on about?
Business is booming right now, son.

32:31.741 --> 32:33.576
What are you going to do
with all that money?

32:33.660 --> 32:35.078
Are you going to take it with you?

32:35.161 --> 32:36.663
I will do M.A.L.F.Y.

32:37.246 --> 32:39.165
Don't you worry about a thing, Ung.

32:39.248 --> 32:42.835
I'll be sure to take
every single cent. You can count on it.

32:44.295 --> 32:45.713
Hey, Mom, do you agree with this?

32:45.797 --> 32:48.174
About this family's legacy?

32:48.257 --> 32:51.970
Well, I'm not sure
about handing it down to you.

32:52.053 --> 32:56.391
Huh? But I'm the only one
who can inherit it. How can you not know?

32:56.474 --> 32:59.769
I think we can trust Yeon-su
to take care of it, am I right?

32:59.852 --> 33:04.107
Yup, that's right. We can trust Yeon-su
to do a much better job than you.

33:04.190 --> 33:05.650
Hmm.

33:05.733 --> 33:06.943
You're so harsh.

33:07.026 --> 33:08.903
Are you saying
you like Yeon-su more than me?

33:08.987 --> 33:09.904
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

33:10.697 --> 33:11.572
That's too bad.

33:12.949 --> 33:14.951
Because she likes me.

33:17.495 --> 33:19.914
I can't believe what I just heard.

33:19.998 --> 33:22.583
I heard it too.
I almost caused an accident.

33:22.667 --> 33:24.585
In fact, I nearly puked on my son's face.

33:28.006 --> 33:31.009
Tell Yeon-su to come over for dinner
when she gets off work.

33:31.092 --> 33:32.093
No, wait a minute.

33:32.677 --> 33:34.429
She might feel pressured by us.

33:35.013 --> 33:37.515
Right. She'll feel pressured
if we keep asking her over.

33:37.598 --> 33:39.350
Should we pack her some side dishes?

33:39.434 --> 33:41.644
That's way she'll have
something to eat with her grandmother.

33:41.728 --> 33:43.646
No, we'll drop by next time.

33:43.730 --> 33:45.815
Yeon-su said she wanted
to eat your braised fish again.

33:45.898 --> 33:47.525
Really? Woo-hoo!

33:47.608 --> 33:48.901
Then tell me when you'll come.

33:48.985 --> 33:51.154
I'll make sure
it's fresh and delicious, just for her.

33:51.988 --> 33:53.489
Does that mean
I should go to the market tomorrow?

33:54.073 --> 33:54.907
Hold on.

33:54.991 --> 33:58.327
Should I get her some side dishes?

34:04.417 --> 34:05.835
Did she leave the lights on?

34:07.795 --> 34:10.256
LEEZAKAYA

34:14.052 --> 34:14.969
Sol-i?

34:15.970 --> 34:16.971
Sol-i, are you here?

34:17.889 --> 34:19.432
Who is that? Eun-ho?

34:19.515 --> 34:21.142
Oh, you're still in.

34:21.225 --> 34:22.852
I thought you said you're closed today.

34:22.935 --> 34:26.522
Yeah. I'm just came in here
to organize some things, that's all.

34:26.606 --> 34:27.732
What are you doing here?

34:27.815 --> 34:31.110
I saw the lights were on from outside,
I thought you forgot to turn them off.

34:31.194 --> 34:33.488
Hey, don't treat me
like I'm some old lady.

34:33.571 --> 34:35.615
I don't forget things that often.

34:35.698 --> 34:38.201
I turned off the lights for you
five times this month.

34:38.993 --> 34:40.995
I do appreciate that…

34:44.624 --> 34:47.126
Rude. Way too rude.

34:47.210 --> 34:49.295
Spitting out water in front of me?

34:49.378 --> 34:52.965
Oh… Why… why are you dressed like that?

34:53.674 --> 34:55.635
Okay, repeat after me.

34:55.718 --> 34:59.013
"Sol-i, why do you look
prettier than usual?"

35:00.056 --> 35:01.849
Where are you going?

35:01.933 --> 35:03.976
What's going on? You're scaring me.

35:04.060 --> 35:07.730
I never thought that
my blind date outfit would ever scare you.

35:07.814 --> 35:09.774
A blind date? You're going on a date?

35:13.277 --> 35:14.403
Who are you going out with?

35:14.487 --> 35:16.906
I don't know yet. My dad's setting me up.

35:17.532 --> 35:19.450
Although I hear he's handsome.

35:20.493 --> 35:21.661
So it's all good.

35:23.329 --> 35:26.499
If your dad's setting you up,
I guess he wants you to marry him.

35:27.041 --> 35:28.584
There's no pressure.

35:31.420 --> 35:34.257
I guess it must feel pretty awkward, huh?

35:34.841 --> 35:37.718
Why awkward? I think it'll be really fun.

35:37.802 --> 35:40.304
How is it fun to eat
with someone you don't know?

35:40.388 --> 35:43.099
Because I love meeting strangers.
It's pretty fun.

35:43.182 --> 35:46.060
Still awkward.
And there's nothing to talk about.

35:46.144 --> 35:49.480
How do I put this? It's my calling.

35:49.564 --> 35:52.275
I have made such good connections
with the people I've just met.

35:52.900 --> 35:55.027
I'd say the flow is incredible.

36:01.159 --> 36:02.994
Hey, I see your mouth.

36:03.661 --> 36:06.497
Okay, tell me.
Why are you pouting this time?

36:06.581 --> 36:10.084
If you keep acting like that,
you'll make me misunderstand you.

36:10.168 --> 36:13.588
I used to be a romance screen writer.
So don't mess with me.

36:15.423 --> 36:17.383
What kind of misunderstanding, huh?

36:17.466 --> 36:20.720
Wow, look at you trying to act naive.

36:20.803 --> 36:23.181
I think I already told you about 35 times.

36:24.473 --> 36:26.225
I don't date younger guys.

36:34.567 --> 36:37.945
Yeah, I know that.
This is my 35th rejection.

36:38.029 --> 36:39.197
Hm?

36:43.659 --> 36:46.078
Go ahead.
You go and have fun with your date.

36:48.039 --> 36:49.498
Oh… okay.

36:51.959 --> 36:55.588
Hold on, let me ask. How old is that guy?

36:56.339 --> 37:00.134
- He's much older than me.
- What's so good about an old guy?

37:03.471 --> 37:05.389
What a rude brat.

37:09.352 --> 37:10.937
Yeah?

37:13.356 --> 37:15.942
I'm taking orders for lunch.
Want anything?

37:16.025 --> 37:17.735
I'm fine. You can eat without me.

37:18.527 --> 37:21.197
- But still you…
- I said I'm fine.

37:22.031 --> 37:23.074
All right.

37:34.710 --> 37:36.671
Hey, you should at least have dinner.

37:36.754 --> 37:39.548
I don't want to eat.
Thanks for asking, though.

37:40.341 --> 37:41.384
But even so--

37:41.467 --> 37:43.844
Don't worry.
I'll eat something later, I promise.

38:04.198 --> 38:06.033
I said I'm not hungry.

38:06.117 --> 38:08.911
Even so,
you should still eat something, Mr. Kim.

38:16.627 --> 38:18.421
I came to see if you were really that busy

38:18.504 --> 38:21.590
or if you were just pretending
so you could get away from me.

38:22.174 --> 38:24.593
I didn't think you would go
as far as skipping meals.

38:25.594 --> 38:28.264
- How'd you get in here?
- I took a taxi, of course.

38:28.347 --> 38:29.807
That's not what I meant--

38:29.890 --> 38:31.726
Well, you should have
answered my messages then.

38:32.852 --> 38:34.645
Are you too busy?
Should I go wait outside?

38:34.729 --> 38:36.480
Oh, no. I'm fine.

38:37.315 --> 38:39.150
All right then. Let's go eat dinner.

38:41.652 --> 38:42.528
Get up now.

38:47.074 --> 38:49.493
Can you wait outside for a second?

38:49.577 --> 38:50.536
Okay.

39:01.297 --> 39:04.425
Wow.
I wish our company had a cafeteria.

39:04.508 --> 39:05.885
You're so lucky.

39:16.354 --> 39:18.230
This is good.

39:18.314 --> 39:21.233
How come you don't eat
all this delicious food? What a waste.

39:21.317 --> 39:24.070
If I worked here,
I'd be eating every single meal here.

39:29.950 --> 39:32.620
By the way, you look like
you lost some weight.

39:33.162 --> 39:34.705
You really haven't been eating?

39:35.623 --> 39:38.626
Tae-hun told me you've been
living in the editing room lately.

39:39.960 --> 39:41.670
Well, I've been busy these days.

39:42.546 --> 39:45.132
I guess being a producer is really tough.

39:45.216 --> 39:48.260
Still, you should eat properly.
We're not young anymore, after all.

39:48.344 --> 39:49.387
Mm.

39:52.348 --> 39:54.183
So why did you come here?

39:55.393 --> 39:59.355
Oh, well, I wanted to ask
if we could check the footage.

39:59.438 --> 40:02.358
Because the footage that you took
about Soen and our project

40:02.441 --> 40:04.527
should have to be checked
with our client first.

40:07.363 --> 40:10.950
- Okay, I'll send it to you.
- Can't I just see it while I'm still here?

40:11.450 --> 40:12.993
I admit, I'm a bit curious.

40:14.161 --> 40:16.414
Um, I don't have much to show you.

40:16.497 --> 40:18.958
I heard the draft for episode one is out.

40:19.041 --> 40:21.210
I haven't made the revisions yet.

40:26.173 --> 40:28.426
- Hey, Ji-ung.
- Hmm?

40:29.009 --> 40:30.553
Why aren't you looking at me?

40:44.525 --> 40:46.193
I look awful right now.

40:47.570 --> 40:50.531
And why would you be worried about that?

40:50.614 --> 40:52.074
Remember your birthday?

40:52.158 --> 40:54.952
I hung out with you
even when my eyes were all swollen.

40:55.786 --> 40:57.329
I hope you didn't forget.

40:57.955 --> 40:58.998
Right.

41:05.337 --> 41:06.755
So, how have you been?

41:08.424 --> 41:11.177
Um. I've been okay.

41:14.346 --> 41:16.932
Same as usual.

41:17.808 --> 41:20.394
And you? Have you been well?

41:20.978 --> 41:23.689
Same as usual for me too.

41:35.910 --> 41:40.080
If I ignore his messages, I'll just seem
even more pathetic and uncool.

41:40.164 --> 41:42.833
I'll just answer him casually,

41:42.917 --> 41:44.460
make it look like I'm fine.

41:45.586 --> 41:46.420
Oh, no.

41:47.671 --> 41:50.049
How deep did I put that thing? Oh!

41:50.674 --> 41:53.511
I should think before I do anything!

42:03.687 --> 42:06.482
Oh, I give up.

42:12.404 --> 42:15.324
- Hey, it seems quite late already.
- Uh.

42:17.993 --> 42:20.037
It's still so early, though.

42:20.120 --> 42:22.331
I guess I had so fun talking to you

42:22.414 --> 42:24.041
that I did not notice the time.

42:25.084 --> 42:26.669
I never expected

42:26.752 --> 42:29.880
that I'd have so much fun
going out on a blind date with someone.

42:29.964 --> 42:31.757
Right?

42:32.508 --> 42:36.345
If it's okay, I would like
to talk with you a little more.

42:39.098 --> 42:40.558
I would love that.

42:41.642 --> 42:42.893
Where do you wanna go?

42:44.019 --> 42:46.647
- There's a place with clam stew--
- How about a cafe?

42:46.730 --> 42:49.108
A cafe sounds nice. Sure, let's go.

42:50.109 --> 42:50.943
Oh, wait.

42:51.026 --> 42:52.945
- Were you saying something earlier?
- No.

42:53.988 --> 42:55.656
The clam stew…

42:58.284 --> 43:00.744
The clams!

43:05.541 --> 43:08.711
Oh, man. Did I forget to lock up again?

43:09.295 --> 43:11.171
What is wrong with me?

43:12.089 --> 43:13.674
Now where are those clams?

43:14.425 --> 43:15.884
Oh, my goodness!

43:15.968 --> 43:18.345
You startled me, Sol-i. Why did you shout?

43:18.429 --> 43:20.306
What the heck was that, huh?

43:20.389 --> 43:23.350
What do you mean? What are you doing here?

43:23.434 --> 43:26.312
You see what I mean?
You forgot about all these clams.

43:26.854 --> 43:28.105
Did you bring these inside?

43:28.188 --> 43:29.648
They were just sitting there outside.

43:29.732 --> 43:32.026
I could have ignored them,
but I decided to be nice.

43:32.109 --> 43:33.861
These clams would've died out there

43:33.944 --> 43:36.322
because you were preoccupied
with your date.

43:44.288 --> 43:45.998
So why are you back early?

43:46.081 --> 43:48.292
You acted like
you were going to have a blast.

43:48.375 --> 43:50.210
It wasn't that fun, wasn't it?

43:50.836 --> 43:53.255
Wasn't it awkward
to talk with a guy you just met?

43:57.676 --> 43:59.386
You were right. It was boring.

44:01.680 --> 44:04.892
You see what I mean?
There was no way it would be any fun.

44:04.975 --> 44:06.018
It was so obvious.

44:06.101 --> 44:09.063
All of your conversations
will just end in silence.

44:09.146 --> 44:10.397
Yeah, you're right.

44:10.481 --> 44:13.609
You know what? You should use that time
to get more customers for this place.

44:13.692 --> 44:15.903
You need to pay back your loan
before you die.

44:18.280 --> 44:20.240
Told you it'd be boring.

44:22.534 --> 44:25.162
I had so much fun today.
Can I see you again next time?

44:26.747 --> 44:28.290
- What's that?
- Oh.

44:29.458 --> 44:30.584
An ad for a loan.

44:30.668 --> 44:34.296
I guess they can really smell people
who are desperate for money.

44:34.380 --> 44:37.007
But do they really send ads at this hour?

44:37.091 --> 44:38.634
They sure work hard.

44:43.681 --> 44:44.932
Do you want clam stew?

44:47.768 --> 44:49.061
Sol-i!

44:49.144 --> 44:51.689
What is it? Why are you yelling?

44:51.772 --> 44:54.441
Do you think you were going to use
my labor for free?

44:55.109 --> 44:56.318
Outrageous.

44:57.111 --> 45:00.406
Anyway, go to the fridge,
I put some of the clams inside.

45:01.865 --> 45:05.160
All right. I'll make you
an amazing clam stew.

45:07.705 --> 45:10.165
And we'll also empty out
my stock of alcohol.

45:10.249 --> 45:13.001
Oh, what? That sounds a bit scary.

45:13.961 --> 45:15.421
Why would we do that?

45:16.714 --> 45:18.590
Hey? Sol-i?

45:24.096 --> 45:25.013
Oh!

45:26.432 --> 45:28.183
I was just about to ring the doorbell.

45:28.267 --> 45:30.978
And I wasn't standing here all night,
so don't get the wrong idea.

45:31.061 --> 45:33.147
Oh, what are you doing here?

45:34.022 --> 45:36.734
I didn't choose to talk
at the interview just for you.

45:36.817 --> 45:38.986
And there was no special meaning to it.

45:39.069 --> 45:42.364
I'm not the kind of person
who'd be so considerate of others.

45:42.448 --> 45:44.658
Oh. Did you come here just to say that?

45:44.742 --> 45:46.160
You could have just
texted me that, you know?

45:46.243 --> 45:47.703
My phone is…

45:48.537 --> 45:51.123
Anyway, it's not what you think.
Do you understand?

45:51.874 --> 45:53.333
You can go inside now.

45:53.417 --> 45:54.835
I was on my way out.

45:54.918 --> 45:56.128
Oh, okay.

45:56.211 --> 45:57.504
Yeah.

46:00.799 --> 46:03.010
Oh, I'm the one who I should leave, right?

46:03.761 --> 46:06.680
Wait, since you came all the way here.
Let me make you tea.

46:08.724 --> 46:09.933
Wait.

46:10.684 --> 46:11.560
Well…

46:13.312 --> 46:14.938
Why don't I give you a ride…

46:15.522 --> 46:16.940
No, that'd be strange too.

46:19.818 --> 46:21.320
I guess that means…

46:22.070 --> 46:23.781
we have an awkward relationship.

46:27.117 --> 46:29.703
I promise I won't visit you randomly
like this anymore.

46:30.287 --> 46:31.580
Nor will I text and call you.

46:31.663 --> 46:33.874
Because if you ask me,
I wouldn't want to see another girl

46:33.957 --> 46:37.461
hovering around my man either.
Especially if it's someone like me,

46:37.544 --> 46:39.421
it'd be quite stressful for her,
don't you think?

46:41.757 --> 46:43.258
We can be…

46:43.759 --> 46:45.928
Never mind.
We are not going to be friends.

46:46.011 --> 46:48.347
'Cause I actually
don't make friends with guys.

46:48.430 --> 46:50.140
So I'm the one who turned you down.

46:50.724 --> 46:53.185
I'll get going, then.
There's no need for you to see me off.

46:58.607 --> 47:00.943
Also, I didn't really like you
that much anyway.

47:01.026 --> 47:02.069
I only liked you a little.

47:02.152 --> 47:05.113
No, in fact, I don't even have
any feelings for you left at all.

47:07.157 --> 47:10.452
But at least let me tell you this,
just in case.

47:11.161 --> 47:12.830
If you break up again, call me.

47:29.721 --> 47:31.473
This is so cool.

47:32.140 --> 47:33.976
I've never seen these.

47:36.270 --> 47:39.231
There's really not much to see.
I still have a lot to work on.

47:39.314 --> 47:40.816
No, it's fine, I understand.

47:40.899 --> 47:42.568
So, what do I press?

48:15.434 --> 48:17.102
PACKED MEALS

48:25.485 --> 48:27.988
Hello. Good day, my name is Choi Ung.

48:30.699 --> 48:31.825
And I am…

48:32.576 --> 48:35.162
Do I really have to do this?

48:35.662 --> 48:38.373
So Ung was actually smirking back then.

48:38.457 --> 48:40.542
Gosh, he's so sly.

48:42.628 --> 48:43.837
Honestly, though,

48:44.588 --> 48:46.882
- I was a bit worried.
- By the way, I don't know

48:46.965 --> 48:50.886
if it's because of
your filming skills or something else,

48:50.969 --> 48:53.472
but I look kind of good.

48:55.974 --> 48:57.225
Huh?

48:58.018 --> 48:59.269
When did you take this?

48:59.353 --> 49:01.063
I didn't know you were still filming.

49:03.065 --> 49:05.275
Wow. I admit,

49:06.109 --> 49:07.945
you're pretty good at your job, huh?

49:08.028 --> 49:10.739
You didn't miss a single moment.

49:15.369 --> 49:19.623
Was I really
looking at Ung with that expression?

49:36.682 --> 49:38.976
- Sorry, Yeon-su, but…
- Huh?

49:39.059 --> 49:42.396
- I have to…
- Oh, right. You're busy.

49:43.021 --> 49:46.566
Sorry.
I took up too much of your time.

49:48.735 --> 49:50.612
Thanks. I enjoyed the video.

49:50.696 --> 49:54.658
I'll send you the file
to your email later.

49:54.741 --> 49:57.744
Okay. Sure. Take good care of your health.

49:59.454 --> 50:01.957
Let's have a good meal with Ung next time.

50:03.458 --> 50:05.293
I don't think I'll be able to
anytime soon.

50:05.377 --> 50:07.045
Do you want to meet near your home?

50:07.129 --> 50:09.006
- Or at Ung's place, or--
- I need some…

50:11.466 --> 50:12.884
I just need some time.

50:13.635 --> 50:14.469
Huh?

50:16.346 --> 50:18.432
I just need some time, that's all.

50:19.474 --> 50:20.726
Oh.

50:21.393 --> 50:23.854
All right. We can meet when you're free.

50:24.521 --> 50:25.981
I'll get going now. Bye.

51:18.867 --> 51:22.204
Yeon-su told me that
she'll be coming home late today.

51:23.205 --> 51:25.290
Oh, I'm aware of that.

51:26.708 --> 51:27.876
So…

51:28.585 --> 51:31.588
you came when you knew
that only I'd be here?

51:31.671 --> 51:33.673
- Yes.
- Well.

51:35.092 --> 51:38.345
You always looked like
a scared little puppy whenever you'd come.

51:38.428 --> 51:39.763
What's the occasion now?

51:42.057 --> 51:44.935
Oh. Well, have you had dinner yet?

51:46.269 --> 51:48.772
- I brought some side dishes.
- I just ate.

51:49.564 --> 51:51.066
I see.

51:53.819 --> 51:55.028
Uh…

52:01.201 --> 52:03.203
- No, stay there.
- Oh.

52:03.286 --> 52:04.830
Let me get you some tea.

52:11.378 --> 52:12.671
Do you like jujube tea?

52:13.880 --> 52:15.465
I love it very much.

52:15.549 --> 52:17.801
I hate it because it smellsso rotten.

52:18.426 --> 52:21.096
Well, good for you.
You can drink everything then.

52:23.098 --> 52:25.392
- Come on. Let's go…
- Right, right.

52:25.475 --> 52:28.061
Come on. Let's go.

52:28.145 --> 52:29.229
Oh, Yeon-su!

52:29.813 --> 52:31.314
Oh, my, did you just get off work?

52:31.398 --> 52:34.442
Yes, I'm on my way home now.
Did you just close up?

52:34.526 --> 52:36.945
Yes, we're about to head
back home ourselves.

52:37.529 --> 52:39.906
- Have you eaten?
- Oh, I just ate with Ji-ung earlier.

52:39.990 --> 52:42.701
- Oh, really?
- So how is Ji-ung doing these days?

52:42.784 --> 52:44.286
We haven't seen him in a long time.

52:44.369 --> 52:47.372
He's been pretty busy.
He hasn't left his office.

52:48.081 --> 52:50.417
We should make some side dishes
for Ji-ung too.

52:50.500 --> 52:51.376
Mm-hmm.

52:51.459 --> 52:55.380
Oh, that's right.
Ung brought some side dishes for you.

52:55.463 --> 52:57.757
- Where did he go?
- To your house, silly.

52:57.841 --> 52:59.259
Didn't he tell you about it?

53:00.218 --> 53:02.512
But, only my grandma is home right now…

53:02.596 --> 53:05.432
You should bring your grandmother along
for a meal next time.

53:05.515 --> 53:08.518
I heard you wanted some braised fish.

53:08.602 --> 53:10.770
I do. Yes. I will.

53:10.854 --> 53:12.272
You must be tired.

53:16.526 --> 53:19.070
Hurry on home. Go get some rest.

53:19.863 --> 53:21.865
Okay. Good night, then.

53:21.948 --> 53:25.619
WITH UNG

53:27.787 --> 53:30.081
Go on. Hurry home.

53:43.470 --> 53:44.512
Where are you?

53:45.138 --> 53:46.348
I heard you went to my house.

53:46.431 --> 53:49.184
Hmm. I was there. I'm back home now.

53:49.267 --> 53:51.686
Uh. Did you meet with my grandmother?

53:51.770 --> 53:54.105
Did she say anything to you? Or scold you?

53:54.189 --> 53:56.900
Actually, wait. I'll go
to your house right now. Wait right there.

53:58.985 --> 54:00.487
I'll make some tea for you.

54:02.113 --> 54:04.866
So then why did you go to my house
while I wasn't there?

54:04.950 --> 54:07.035
You must have been bullied
by my grandma again.

54:07.118 --> 54:08.078
I wasn't.

54:12.874 --> 54:15.001
Do you read books
like this lately?

54:16.795 --> 54:19.756
I haven't been reading much lately. Hm.

54:19.839 --> 54:21.216
I should read more too.

54:29.432 --> 54:31.101
ENSA ENROLLMENT FORM

54:31.184 --> 54:33.019
ARTIST GO-OH
MUSEUM OF AVANT-GARDE, PARIS, FRANCE

54:33.103 --> 54:35.272
CONCERNING VARIABILITY
AND INVARIABILITY›

54:35.355 --> 54:36.398
PROGRAMS, ALUMNI, ENROLLMENT

54:36.481 --> 54:37.941
What's this now?

54:38.024 --> 54:39.734
It's nothing.

54:39.818 --> 54:43.363
This kind of looks like a brochure
for an architecture school.

54:43.446 --> 54:45.490
Were you once interested in architecture?

54:45.573 --> 54:48.660
Well, do you remember the architect
I told you I liked?

54:49.411 --> 54:51.913
He's a professor there,
so I was looking at it.

54:51.997 --> 54:54.207
Oh. Oh, well.

54:54.291 --> 54:57.877
You're always drawing buildings, so
of course you would be interested in it.

54:58.378 --> 55:00.505
- I'm really not.
- Why?

55:00.588 --> 55:02.632
I think it would be nice
for you to learn more.

55:02.716 --> 55:04.592
Why would I do that?

55:04.676 --> 55:06.761
It would be such a bother.

55:06.845 --> 55:09.472
Drawing is exhausting enough as it is.

55:10.056 --> 55:10.974
You're right.

55:11.057 --> 55:13.935
Having a university diploma
is already enough.

55:15.937 --> 55:18.064
- What?
- I didn't graduate.

55:19.482 --> 55:20.400
What?

55:21.443 --> 55:22.360
Why?

55:23.403 --> 55:25.405
I thought I didn't really need to.

55:25.488 --> 55:28.241
Wait, Ung, have you lost your mind?

55:28.325 --> 55:31.202
You attended school
and paid for that tuition.

55:31.286 --> 55:33.163
Are you saying that all went to waste?

55:33.830 --> 55:37.625
Well, you know what?
I never wanted to go to university anyway.

55:37.709 --> 55:39.127
I only went because of you.

55:43.089 --> 55:44.883
Hey, why are you so shocked?

55:44.966 --> 55:47.385
You know very well that
I don't like going to school.

55:49.596 --> 55:53.850
Yeah, but still, how could you
just quit so easily like that?

55:54.934 --> 55:57.979
There are people
who don't really need a diploma.

55:59.439 --> 56:01.149
Is that your reason?

56:01.232 --> 56:03.777
You'll be able to draw
all the buildings you love

56:03.860 --> 56:06.029
and learn much more if you go there.

56:06.112 --> 56:08.490
Give this chance to someone
who needs it more than I do.

56:14.496 --> 56:17.415
Oh, that's right.
Eun-ho bought some cookies. Hang on.

56:21.169 --> 56:24.923
By the way, I want to know
if Grandma said anything to you?

56:25.006 --> 56:28.134
If she said anything harsh to you,
don't take it personally.

56:28.218 --> 56:29.803
It's just her way of talking.

56:38.728 --> 56:41.689
Yeon-su. Can I ask you a question?

56:42.982 --> 56:44.776
Hmm. What is it?

56:47.195 --> 56:48.029
So why…

56:54.035 --> 56:56.287
why did we break up back then?

57:14.180 --> 57:18.977
EPILOGUE

57:23.106 --> 57:26.609
I am so completely messed up.

57:30.280 --> 57:31.656
Here, drink this.

57:32.615 --> 57:33.450
Thanks.

57:35.910 --> 57:39.789
I saw you two
in the editing room a while ago.

57:39.873 --> 57:41.749
It reminded me of a movie.

57:41.833 --> 57:43.001
A movie?

57:43.084 --> 57:44.586
Love Actually.

57:45.170 --> 57:47.714
The story where the guy likes
his best friend's wife.

57:49.340 --> 57:50.675
You sure that's not Love and War?

57:52.177 --> 57:56.264
In the movie's ending, the guy he ends up
confessing his feelings in a sketchbook.

57:57.307 --> 57:59.434
That became it's most famous scene.

58:02.353 --> 58:04.439
What's your ending going to be?

58:06.107 --> 58:07.567
Don't know.

58:07.650 --> 58:09.360
Because mine's not a movie.

58:11.905 --> 58:13.406
It's a documentary.

58:50.985 --> 58:52.445
See, that's what the media does.

58:52.529 --> 58:55.490
It attracts unnecessary attention
as a consequence.

58:55.573 --> 58:56.574
How have you been?

58:56.658 --> 58:58.993
By the way,
why don't you have any friends?

58:59.077 --> 59:01.955
Do you actually think
we're in the same situation?

59:02.539 --> 59:04.916
Just so you know,
Sol-i's not yours anymore.

59:04.999 --> 59:07.168
What kind of person
do I come off as?

59:07.752 --> 59:10.129
Do I look lost and aimless?

59:10.964 --> 59:12.632
That's what
the past does to you.

59:14.133 --> 59:16.386
It causes you to make the same mistakes.

59:16.469 --> 59:20.181
You seemed
so desperate to break up with me.
